  "notes": [
    "Calendar overlays describe nominal celebrations; they do not determine what is observed on a particular year/date.",
    "Do not infer colour, readings, holy-day obligation, or precedence solely from the rank in these records.",
    "Retain all candidates on a date; a separate precedence engine selects the applicable observance.",
    "St Anselm (21 April), St Boniface (5 June), and St Andrew (30 November) already have the appropriate dates/ranks in the universal layer, so no duplicates are needed.",
    "St Fidelis of Sigmaringen remains on 24 April in the universal layer; St Adalbert becomes an additional nominal candidate that day in England."
  ],
